  "notes": "Vocal-driven progressive house and label-runner. The research states the harmonic consequence of his emphasis directly: he is \"known for vocal-driven arrangements\" and co-produces with outside pop artists, \"so the harmony is written to carry a sung topline rather than only an instrumental hook\". That is why this model's melody is a sung-register question-and-answer over 4- and 8-bar phrases rather than the trio's 8/16-bar instrumental anthem, and why \"his productions typically restate the vocal over the second drop\" shows up as a structure that returns to the hook rather than to an instrumental. The kit is progressive house \"with an emphasis on percussion layering across 8- and 16-bar phrases\", so the perc bed is the densest of the three trio members at 3-6 hits a bar, and \"fills are noise sweeps and filtered snare rolls\" gives a riser lane plus an authored roll ramp. Bass is \"sidechained saw; sub muted under breakdowns\". ⚠ The research calls the parameters convention-derived; that mark is repeated here, and every velocity, density and register above is INFERRED.",
